WEBVTT

00:32:27.850 --> 00:32:30.306
But soon enough,
Chris found that firefighting

00:32:30.330 --> 00:32:33.946
was also a quick road
to emotional exhaustion.

00:32:33.970 --> 00:32:35.970
He couldn't control
the calls that came in,

00:32:35.994 --> 00:32:37.927
or the tragedies that endured.

00:32:37.951 --> 00:32:39.496
(Overlapping 911 calls)

00:32:39.520 --> 00:32:41.606
CM: So everybody's gone.

00:32:41.630 --> 00:32:43.935
So open bay.

00:32:43.959 --> 00:32:46.371
Like, where you can see
all the shoes left behind,

00:32:46.395 --> 00:32:49.766
you can tell that that's where the members
jumped on the truck,

00:32:49.790 --> 00:32:51.290
when the truck got their call.

00:32:52.260 --> 00:32:54.902
AG: One minute, he'd be playing
cards in the firehouse.

00:32:54.926 --> 00:32:56.837
The next minute, the siren would go off

00:32:56.861 --> 00:32:58.646
and he'd be racing onto the truck.

00:32:58.670 --> 00:33:01.146
Soon, he'd be running
into a burning building.